{"seq":14,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-verbs-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T17:06:35.752Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"67d1a031fb74c320b26a6689724142df5bf8fc1f94ad603e4d8e0c4b329ddab8","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**: `dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday` (\"Sunday prep for Ruth\", 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct 2025 about kiosk SMS bay assignments at the Eau Claire yard. It's also in the action items for 6 Oct.\n2. **#4419**: `dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet` (\"North cheat sheet\", undated). Thea logged it for gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14. The sheet says it was escalated to tier-2 support.\n3. **#4419**: `dev/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap` (Marcus Lindqvist, 14 Jul 2025). Here the same number is described as \"Gate 3 printer lag\" (bol printout delay), which doesn't match the cheat sheet's description of the same ticket. Someone should check which is right in the ticket system.\n\nI found no QFL ticket numbers in #north-team or #inc-qfl-sev1, which you're in. The \"Quarendon Freightways\" intel note isn't Quarrendon Freight Lines, so I left it out. The search tool is keyword-only, so a note that words its ticket differently could still be missing. If you want, I can take another pass when the weekly notes are ready."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
